course: dictionary
lesson: 15586
title: Synchronisation: moving and matching together
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Synchronisation means making things happen at exactly the same time or speed. The word has a clue inside it: "sync" means together, like two clocks showing the same time. «The swimmers raised their arms in perfect synchronisation, all at the same moment.» The swimmers did not just move; they moved together, at the same time.
explain: Synchronisation is also used for computers and phones. Here it means keeping information the same on two devices, which is often called syncing. «My laptop and my phone show the same photos, because the data is in synchronisation.» If you add a photo on your phone, it appears on your laptop too.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence to know which meaning is used. Dance, swimming and music point to moving together. Phones, laptops and files point to keeping things the same. «The film's sound was out of synchronisation, so the words did not match the actors' lips.» Here out of synchronisation means not at the same time.
fact: Synchronisation is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we do not say "a synchronisation".
fact: «Synchronisation» means making things happen at exactly the same time or speed.
fact: In technology, «synchronisation» means keeping information the same on two devices, and it is often called «syncing».
fact: «Synchronisation» can also be spelled «synchronization», with a z. Both spellings are correct.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «in synchronisation», «synchronisation of clocks» and «data synchronisation».
exercise: «The dancers finished their routine in perfect synchronisation.» What does synchronisation mean here? | Dancing very slowly | Wearing matching costumes | Leaving the stage early | *Moving at exactly the same time
exercise: «My phone and my laptop show the same photos because they sync.» What does sync mean here? | Charging the battery | Deleting old files | *Keeping information the same on two devices | Turning off the screen
exercise: Ben says, «Synchronisation is only for dancers.» Is he right? | No, it means eating dinner together | Yes, but only in science lessons | Yes, only dancers and swimmers use it | *No, it is also used for devices and for film sound
test: «The film's sound was out of synchronisation, so the actors' voices did not match their lips.» What does out of synchronisation mean? | *Not happening at the same time | Very loud | Made in a studio | Turned off
test: Synchronisation can also be spelled in another way. Which spelling is correct? | sinchronisation | synkronisation | *synchronization | synchronisasion
exam: Which sentence is the best example of synchronisation? | A book left on a shelf | *Two swimmers moving their arms at exactly the same moment | A cat sleeping on a sunny windowsill | A bird flying alone across the field
